<title>THAILAND: Thai oil crushers buy 50,000 tonnes U.S. soybean.</title>
<headline>Thai oil crushers buy 50,000 tonnes U.S. soybean.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai oil crushers bought 50,000 tonnes of U.S. soybeans at $298 a tonne for prompt shipment, trade sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A Thai Cottonseed, Ricebran and Vegetable Oil Crushers Association official told Reuters the tender was held on Tuesday. He declined to give further details.</p>
<p>The price for the soybeans was quoted C&amp;F Si Chang, a port in the east of Bangkok.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
